==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|loch}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|louh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*laukaz}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|Look}}, {{m|nds|look}}, Dutch {{m|nl|look}}, English {{m|en|leek}}, Danish {{m|da|løg}}, Swedish {{m|sv|lök}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[laʊ̯χ]|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m||Lauche}}

# [[leek]]

====Usage notes====
''Porree'' is dominant in northern and central Germany, while ''Lauch'' is dominant in southern Germany and Switzerland; in Austria, neither is dominant.

